      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Biological advancements rely heavily on historical inventions, vaccines, and anatomical discoveries.",
        "Gregor Mendel established the fundamental Laws of Heredity through systematic genetics research.",
        "The identification of DNA structure and ABO blood group systems revolutionized modern medicine and genetics.",
        "Biological instruments and laboratory techniques enabled significant breakthroughs in disease prevention and diagnostic health."
      ],
      "id": "u24r579"
