    {
      "id": "x38lz63",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. DNA Discovery"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cs9k3tm",
      "content": "DNA was first isolated by Friedrich Miescher in 1869. The double helix structure was proposed by James Watson and Francis Crick in 1953 based on X-ray diffraction data of Rosalind Franklin."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 16: INVENTIONS & DISCOVERIES IN BIOLOGY",
      "id": "8rpkof8"
    },
    {
      "id": "lqatjlv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Blood Group Discovery"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8btig93",
      "content": "Karl Landsteiner discovered the ABO blood group system in 1900. He also co-discovered the Rh factor later."
    },
