    {
      "id": "uwb0v1m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Laws of Heredity (Gregor Mendel)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iux8ocu",
      "content": "Gregor Mendel proposed three laws of heredity based on pea plant experiments."
    },
    {
      "id": "8npp46i",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Law</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Statement</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Dominance</p>",
            "<p>Dominant trait masks recessive trait.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Segregation</p>",
            "<p>Alleles separate during gamete formation.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Law of Independent Assortment</p>",
            "<p>Traits assort independently.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
